On Fri, 22 Sep 2006, Rast wrote:
>
> In wizmode, wish for fireproof bag of holding, ring of levitation.
> Levitate, then wish for "lava".  Drop bag -- it burns up.
>
> Bug?

   Definitely, in at least two ways, AFAICT.

   (1) Fireproof /anything/ shouldn't catch fire and burn up when dropped
into lava, IMHO, although I could see an argument here --- lava might be
considered a very powerful form of fire that can't be resisted.

   (2) A continuation of (1): From the source code, I got the impression
that fireproofing containers doesn't change their likelihood of burning
up --- it's always chance(20) for bags. Maybe it works correctly for
non-container objects; I didn't look closely.

   (3) The behavior Rast describes is not the same behavior you get when
you water-walk onto the lava and drop the bag. In fact, it looks like
generally dropping anything onto lava from a height has totally different
effects from dropping the same thing from a standing position. This seems
totally wrong, except for a few obvious special cases such as mirrors
shattering when they hit the ground from a height.

-Arthur


